{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":87,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidWordHolonomy_cyclic_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidWordHolonomy_cyclic_one","kind":"theorem","line":740,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L740-L760","doc":"**Closed-braid (Markov-closure) holonomy is conjugation-stable.**\nA braid word and any cyclic permutation of its letters yield\nboundary holonomies that are conjugate in `G` (the Markov-trace\nclosure is a *class function*, invariant under conjugation).  We\nprove the one-letter rotation case: rotating the first letter `g`\nto the end conjugates the holonomy by `g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidSurfaceMultTrace_eq_braidWordHolonomy_replicate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidSurfaceMultTrace_eq_braidWordHolonomy_replicate","kind":"theorem","line":727,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L727-L738","doc":"**Toy model is the single-letter special case.**  The original\nscalar model `braidSurfaceMultTrace z n = z ^ n` IS the boundary\nholonomy of the braid word `[z, z, …, z]` (`n` copies of the same\nHecke-image generator `z`).  So the real ordered-product holonomy\n`braidWordHolonomy` strictly generalises the toy: the toy is\nrecovered exactly when every letter of the word is the same\ngenerator `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidWordHolonomy_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidWordHolonomy_append","kind":"theorem","line":718,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L718-L725","doc":"**Concatenation of braid words.**  The boundary holonomy of a\nconcatenated braid word is the product of the two holonomies —\nfunctoriality of the holonomy under braid composition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidWordHolonomy_append_letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidWordHolonomy_append_letter","kind":"theorem","line":708,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L708-L716","doc":"**Markov cocycle (append a generator).**  Appending one more\nHecke-image letter `g` to a braid word multiplies its boundary\nholonomy on the right by `g` — the non-abelian Markov-axiom\nrecursion `Hol(β · σ_i) = Hol(β) · ρ(σ_i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidWordHolonomy_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidWordHolonomy_nil","kind":"theorem","line":703,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L703-L706","doc":"The empty braid word's boundary holonomy is the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidWordHolonomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidWordHolonomy","kind":"def","line":692,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L692-L701","doc":"**Braid-word boundary holonomy.**  For a braid word presented as a\nlist of its Hecke-image generator-actions `[ρ(σ_{i₁}), …,\nρ(σ_{i_ℓ})] : List G`, the boundary holonomy of the Seifert\nsurface is the left-ordered product `ρ(σ_{i₁}) · ⋯ · ρ(σ_{i_ℓ})`.\nThis is the genuine non-abelian Stokes boundary holonomy (the\nsurface-ordered exponential reduces to the ordered product on the\npiecewise-affine Young-diagram surface), replacing the toy scalar\npower `z ^ ℓ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.yekutieli_stokes_continuous_path","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.yekutieli_stokes_continuous_path","kind":"theorem","line":663,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L663-L672","doc":"**Yekutieli-Stokes for the continuous-path pairing**: the\nline integral over the boundary of a 2-cell agrees with the\nsurface-integral pairing.  On the skeleton, both sides equal\n1 by definition; the genuine analytic identity is the\nupstream target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.continuousPath2FormPairing_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.continuousPath2FormPairing_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":657,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L657-L661","doc":"The continuous-path 2-form pairing is identity-valued on the\nskeleton. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.continuousPath2FormPairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.continuousPath2FormPairing","kind":"def","line":648,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L648-L655","doc":"**Continuous-path 2-form pairing (skeleton)**: a placeholder\nfor the `MI₂` evaluation on a continuous (non-piecewise-affine)\n2-cell.  Concrete model: the constant-1 surface integral.\nThis bridges the piecewise-affine finite-slice case to the\nYekutieli continuous-path framework that Mathlib's\ndifferential-forms library is the upstream target for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_three_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_three_step","kind":"theorem","line":596,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L596-L601","doc":"**Three-step holonomy**: integrating `[g, h, k]` is `g · h · k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_two_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_two_step","kind":"theorem","line":589,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L589-L594","doc":"**Two-step holonomy**: integrating `[g, h]` is `g · h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_one_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_one_step","kind":"theorem","line":584,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L584-L587","doc":"**Single-step holonomy**: integrating `[g]` is `g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_append_assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_append_assoc","kind":"theorem","line":576,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L576-L582","doc":"**Concatenation associativity**: piecewise-affine line integral\nbehaves associatively under three-way concatenation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_append_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_append_nil","kind":"theorem","line":568,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L568-L574","doc":"**Concatenation identity-right**: appending an empty path\nleaves the integral unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_nil_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_nil_append","kind":"theorem","line":560,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L560-L566","doc":"**Concatenation identity-left**: prepending an empty path\nleaves the integral unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_reverse_inverse_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_reverse_inverse_pair","kind":"theorem","line":547,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L547-L558","doc":"**Reverse-and-invert closure**: integrating the reverse list of\ninverses yields the inverse of the original integral.\n\nFor a path `[g₁, g₂, …, gₙ]` with integral `∏ = g₁·g₂·⋯·gₙ`,\nthe inverse path `[gₙ⁻¹, …, g₂⁻¹, g₁⁻¹]` integrates to `∏⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_replicate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_replicate","kind":"theorem","line":529,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L529-L545","doc":"**Replicate path holonomy**: integrating the same generator `n`\ntimes gives `g^n`.  Connects piecewise-affine path integration\nto the natural-number power on the group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.yekutieli_markov_axiom_via_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.yekutieli_markov_axiom_via_split","kind":"theorem","line":512,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L512-L521","doc":"**`YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace` instance commutes with\n`braidSurfaceMultTrace_add_split`**: the Markov axiom\n`tr_M(x · σ_n) = z · tr_M(x)` follows by setting `m = ℓ(x)`\nand `k = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.finite_slice_trace_at_depth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.finite_slice_trace_at_depth","kind":"theorem","line":506,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L506-L510","doc":"**Finite-slice trace explicit formula** at depth k:\n`tr_M(σ^k) = z^k` for any single-generator braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidSurfaceMultTrace_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidSurfaceMultTrace_identity","kind":"theorem","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L501-L504","doc":"**Holonomy of identity braid**: `tr_M(1) = z^0 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidSurfaceMultTrace_add_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidSurfaceMultTrace_add_split","kind":"theorem","line":492,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L492-L499","doc":"**`braidSurfaceMultTrace` is `z`-multiplicative**: at\n`n = m + k`, the trace decomposes as `z^m * z^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.closedPathHolonomy_two_pairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.closedPathHolonomy_two_pairs","kind":"theorem","line":484,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L484-L490","doc":"**Generator-pair holonomy**: a closed path `[g, g⁻¹, h, h⁻¹]`\nintegrates to 1 (two cancelling pairs). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.closedPathHolonomy_via_inverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.closedPathHolonomy_via_inverse","kind":"theorem","line":475,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L475-L482","doc":"**Closed path holonomy**: for a path expressed as a list\nof generator actions returning to the identity (closed\nloop), the multiplicative line integral equals 1.  This\nis the \"trivially closed loop\" Yekutieli identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes_canonical","kind":"def","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L446-L466","doc":"**The zero model**: `α = 0`, `β = 0`, both integrals constantly `0`.\n\nA `def`, not an `instance`, for the reason recorded at `punitInstance`: a\nglobal instance discharges every downstream `[LieValuedStokes …]` behind\nits author's back.  A caller wanting it writes\n`letI := LieValuedStokes_canonical M 𝔤`.\n\nWhat it establishes is consistency and nothing more.  By the `qou-z9ws`\ninhabitation discriminator, a model in which every integral is `0` is\nevidence the axioms can be satisfied and no evidence that they constrain\nanything; a non-degenerate model needs the analytic theory this file\nabstracts away, and `qou-ewc4` stays open for it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.stokes_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.stokes_identity","kind":"theorem","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L422-L422","doc":"**Yekutieli-Stokes, infinitesimal form**: `∫_{∂σ} α = ∫_σ d_α β`, with\n`d_α β` the `gaugeCovariantDerivative` defined above.\n\nThis is bean `qou-ewc4`, filed by\n`UpstreamSubstrateBridge.lean` when it REMOVED a\n`∃ S : LieValuedStokes M 𝔤, True` rather than restate it: *\"making the\ncarrier content-bearing (a real `stokes_identity` field rather than a\n`Prop` + witness pair)\"*.  That is this field.  The three integrals it\nquantifies over are carried because this class had the forms and no way\nto integrate them, which is why it could not state its own subject. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.boundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.boundary","kind":"def","line":411,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L411-L411","doc":"The boundary `∂σ` of a 2-cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.surfaceIntegral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.surfaceIntegral","kind":"def","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L409-L409","doc":"Surface integral of a 2-form over a 2-cell, valued in `𝔤`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.lineIntegral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.lineIntegral","kind":"def","line":407,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L407-L407","doc":"Line integral of a 1-form along a path, valued in `𝔤`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.beta","kind":"def","line":405,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L405-L405","doc":"The 2-form `β`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.alpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.alpha","kind":"def","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L403-L403","doc":"The 1-form `α`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes.mk","kind":"ctor","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L400-L400","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedStokes","kind":"class","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L397-L424","doc":"**Class hypothesis**: a Lie-valued non-abelian Stokes\nframework.  Bundles the 1-form, 2-form, gauge-covariant\nderivative, and the Yekutieli-Stokes identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.gaugeCovariantDerivative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.gaugeCovariantDerivative","kind":"def","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L386-L395","doc":"The **gauge-covariant derivative** `d_α β = dβ + [α, β]`\nappearing in Yekutieli-Stokes.  Abstract here as a function\nof the underlying 1-form `α` and 2-form `β`; concrete\ninstance requires the manifold + Lie-algebra structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraTwoForm.eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraTwoForm.eval","kind":"def","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L384-L384","doc":"The underlying bivector-evaluation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraTwoForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraTwoForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":382,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L382-L382","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraTwoForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraTwoForm","kind":"structure","line":381,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L381-L384","doc":"**Lie-valued 2-form**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraOneForm.eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraOneForm.eval","kind":"def","line":379,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L379-L379","doc":"The underlying form-evaluation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraOneForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraOneForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L377-L377","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraOneForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraOneForm","kind":"structure","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L376-L379","doc":"**Lie-valued 1-form** as an abstract function `M → 𝔤`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.bracket_antisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.bracket_antisym","kind":"theorem","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L359-L374","doc":"Antisymmetry corollary: `[x, y] = -[y, x]`.\n\nDerivation: `[x+y, x+y] = 0` (by `bracket_self`); expand\nvia bilinearity to `[x,x] + [x,y] + [y,x] + [y,y] = 0`;\napply `bracket_self` to drop `[x,x]` and `[y,y]`; conclude\n`[x,y] + [y,x] = 0`, i.e. `[x,y] = -[y,x]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure.jacobi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure.jacobi","kind":"theorem","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L355-L355","doc":"Jacobi identity: `[[x,y],z] + [[y,z],x] + [[z,x],y] = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure.bracket_add_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure.bracket_add_right","kind":"theorem","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L352-L352","doc":"Bilinearity (right): `[x, y + z] = [x, y] + [x, z]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure.bracket_add_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure.bracket_add_left","kind":"theorem","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L349-L349","doc":"Bilinearity (left): `[x + y, z] = [x, z] + [y, z]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure.bracket_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure.bracket_self","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L347-L347","doc":"Antisymmetry on the diagonal: `[x, x] = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure.bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure.bracket","kind":"def","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L345-L345","doc":"The Lie bracket. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L343-L343","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieAlgebraStructure","kind":"class","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L339-L357","doc":"**Lie algebra structure** as an abstract class.  In Mathlib\nproper, this is `LieAlgebra k 𝔤`; here we re-export the\nbracket axioms (with bilinearity) that the Yekutieli-Stokes\nproof requires. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.yekutieli_finite_slice_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.yekutieli_finite_slice_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L303-L325","doc":"**Substrate theorem** (S-Yekutieli-finite-slice).  At finite slice\ndepth, the multiplicative integral on a Young-diagram braid surface\nIS a finite product of generator-actions: **any** multiplicative\ntrace satisfying the two finite-slice axioms is the `n`-fold product\n`z ^ n`.\n\nQuantified over an arbitrary `Y`, so both class axioms are\nload-bearing (`trace_zero` in the base case, `trace_succ` in the\nstep) and a trace differing from `z ^ n` at any `n` would refute it.\nContrast the canonical instance, for which `trace n = z ^ n` holds\nby `rfl` (`finite_slice_trace_at_depth`) and therefore says nothing:\nthe content here is that the axioms *determine* the trace, not that\none chosen model satisfies them.\n\nSee the \"Substrate theorem\" note above for what this replaced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace_canonical","kind":"instance","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L295-L301","doc":"**Canonical instance** of `YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace`\nusing `braidSurfaceMultTrace` directly.  Concrete; not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace.trace_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace.trace_succ","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L293-L293","doc":"Markov-axiom recursion: trace at length `n+1` is `z`\ntimes the trace at length `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace.trace_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace.trace_zero","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L290-L290","doc":"Normalisation: trace at length 0 is the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace.trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace.trace","kind":"def","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L288-L288","doc":"The trace value for a braid of given Coxeter length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L286-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace","kind":"class","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L281-L293","doc":"**`YekutieliFiniteSliceMultTrace` class** (substantive\nversion): provides the per-braid-word multiplicative trace\nas a class field, plus the Markov-axiom cocycle.  Concrete\ninstances at small braid lengths discharge by direct\ncomputation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.stokes_trivial_case","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.stokes_trivial_case","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L273-L279","doc":"**Stokes identity** for the trivial case: on a trivial\nsurface (no boundary), both line and surface integrals\nreduce to the identity.  This is the simplest non-vacuous\ncase of `stokes_holds`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidSurfaceMultTrace_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidSurfaceMultTrace_succ","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L266-L271","doc":"**Markov-axiom-style cocycle**: appending a generator to a\nbraid multiplies the Markov trace by `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidSurfaceMultTrace_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidSurfaceMultTrace_zero","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L260-L264","doc":"Empty braid trace: `tr_M(1) = z⁰ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidSurfaceMultTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.braidSurfaceMultTrace","kind":"def","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L252-L258","doc":"**Braid-surface multiplicative trace**: for a braid word\nexpressed as a list of generators, the trace of the closed\nbraid is the multiplicative line integral over the closure\npath.  Concretely modelled as a function of the braid word's\nCoxeter length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_inverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_inverse","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L245-L250","doc":"**Inverse-pair closure**: a path followed by its inverse\nintegrates to the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_append","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L236-L243","doc":"**Concatenation rule**: the line integral of a concatenated\npath is the product of the individual integrals. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.foldl_mul_distributes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.foldl_mul_distributes","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L224-L234","doc":"**Helper**: `foldl (· * ·) a` distributes over the base\nmultiplication, i.e. `l.foldl (· * ·) a = a * l.foldl\n(· * ·) 1`.  Standard monoid lemma; proved by induction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L218-L222","doc":"The line integral of a single generator is that generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.finite_slice_eq_piecewiseAffine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.finite_slice_eq_piecewiseAffine","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L209-L216","doc":"The `NonAbelianStokes.finite_slice` field's right-hand side IS\n`piecewiseAffineLineIntegral` of the slice.  The field is spelled as the\nraw fold only because this definition lands below the class; recording the\nidentification here keeps the axiom readable as what it means. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral_nil","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L205-L207","doc":"The empty path's line integral is the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.piecewiseAffineLineIntegral","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L197-L203","doc":"**Piecewise-affine line integral**: for a list of generator\nactions `g₁, g₂, …, gₖ : G`, the multiplicative line integral\nis the left-ordered product `g₁ · g₂ · ⋯ · gₖ`.  This is the\nQOU-substrate's finite-slice realisation of `MI₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.punitInstance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.punitInstance","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L125-L158","doc":"**Skeleton model** — both multiplicative integrals are constantly\n`1` and both `Prop` fields are `True`.  It encodes no Stokes\nidentity and no finite-slice reduction.  Genuine models over\n`M = ℝ²`, `G = SU(n)`, etc., arrive once Mathlib's\nLie-valued-forms library lands.\n\n**A `def`, not an `instance`, since 2026-08-24.**  This file's own\nprose at §\"Substrate theorem\" already named the defect: because\n`NonAbelianStokes` pairs `stokes_holds : Prop` with\n`stokes_holds_witness : stokes_holds`, it is a *self-certifying\ncarrier*, inhabited by taking the `Prop` to be `True` — *\"which\n`punitInstance` below literally does\"*.  That was written to\njustify restating a `∃ (_ : NonAbelianStokes M G), True` claim\nagainst real content; the instance it names was left resolvable, so\nany future `[NonAbelianStokes M G]` hypothesis would still have\nbeen discharged with `True` before its author noticed.\n\nBlast radius of the demotion, measured: **zero** — no declaration\nin the corpus takes `[NonAbelianStokes M G]`.  A caller wanting the\nskeleton writes `letI := punitInstance M G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.finite_slice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.finite_slice","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L122-L122","doc":"**Finite-slice axiom**: on a piecewise-affine surface the\nmultiplicative integral IS the finite generator product.\n\nWritten as the fold rather than as `piecewiseAffineLineIntegral (slice\nγ)` only because that definition lands below this class in the file;\n`finite_slice_eq_piecewiseAffine` immediately after it records that the\ntwo are the same, so the link is stated rather than left to the reader\nto notice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.stokes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.stokes","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L110-L110","doc":"**Yekutieli-Stokes identity**: `MI₁(α; ∂σ) = MI₂(α, d_α β; σ)`.\n\nWas `stokes_holds : Prop` with a sibling witness — a field typed with\nthe UNIVERSE `Prop`, so the instance supplied both the proposition and\nits proof.  Its own docstring called itself a \"placeholder Prop\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.slice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.slice","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L104-L104","doc":"The piecewise-affine slicing of a path into finitely many generator\nactions.  A field for the same reason as `boundary`: the finite-slice\naxiom is a statement ABOUT such a decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.covariantD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.covariantD","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L99-L99","doc":"The gauge-covariant derivative `d_α β = dβ + [α, β]` at the level of the\ngroup-valued forms this class works with.  (`gaugeCovariantDerivative`\nbelow is the Lie-algebra-valued counterpart.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.boundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.boundary","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L95-L95","doc":"The boundary `∂σ` of a 2-cell, as a path.  A field because this file\nabstracts the manifold away; stating Stokes needs a boundary and there\nwas none to refer to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.surfaceIntegral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.surfaceIntegral","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The surface integral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.lineIntegral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.lineIntegral","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The line integral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes.mk","kind":"ctor","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.NonAbelianStokes","kind":"class","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L76-L123","doc":"**Yekutieli's non-abelian Stokes** as a §3b-cond class.\n\nThe class fields encode the integral-equality content of\nYekutieli (2015):\n  `MI₁(α; ∂σ) = MI₂(d_α β; σ)`\nwhere `d_α β = dβ + [α, β]` is the gauge-covariant derivative.\n\nFor the QOU substrate, the **finite-slice** version applies\non the piecewise-affine Young-diagram braid surface: every\nmultiplicative integral is a literal finite product of\ngenerator-actions; no analytic limit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.MultiplicativeSurfaceIntegral.integrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.MultiplicativeSurfaceIntegral.integrate","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The surface-integral-evaluation map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.MultiplicativeSurfaceIntegral.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.MultiplicativeSurfaceIntegral.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.MultiplicativeSurfaceIntegral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.MultiplicativeSurfaceIntegral","kind":"structure","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L68-L74","doc":"The **multiplicative surface integral** `MI₂(α, β; σ) ∈ G`\nof a 2-form `β` (with auxiliary 1-form `α`) over a 2-cell\n`σ`.  Abstracted as a function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.MultiplicativeLineIntegral.integrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.MultiplicativeLineIntegral.integrate","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L66-L66","doc":"The integral-evaluation map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.MultiplicativeLineIntegral.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.MultiplicativeLineIntegral.mk","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.MultiplicativeLineIntegral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.MultiplicativeLineIntegral","kind":"structure","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L60-L66","doc":"The **multiplicative line integral** `MI₁(α; γ) ∈ G` of\na Lie-valued 1-form `α` along a path `γ`.  Defined as\nthe limit of left-ordered products of `exp(α(γ'(t_i)) Δt)`\nin the genuine theory; abstracted here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedTwoForm.eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedTwoForm.eval","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The underlying form-evaluation map (pointwise on\ntangent bivectors). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedTwoForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedTwoForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedTwoForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedTwoForm","kind":"structure","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L54-L58","doc":"Abstract carrier for a Lie-algebra-valued 2-form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedOneForm.eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedOneForm.eval","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The underlying form-evaluation map (concrete instance:\npointwise tangent-vector evaluation into 𝔤). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedOneForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedOneForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedOneForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.NonAbelianStokes.LieValuedOneForm","kind":"structure","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/NonAbelianStokes.lean#L45-L52","doc":"Abstract carrier for a Lie-algebra-valued 1-form on a\nmanifold `M` with values in a Lie group `G`.  Concrete\ninstances would be `Ω¹(M; 𝔤)` from the Mathlib geometry\nlibrary. ","signatureChunk":0}]}